{"id":"case-5fea6da992bdb6","assertion":"OpenProse externalizes control flow and state while execution remains LLM-mediated, yielding scoping benefits before hard reliability.","follow":"B explains why flat context lacks local bindings, isolation, and capture protection.","reconsider_rejected":"The claimed scoping gain and intermediate regime would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's account of context isolation would require updating A's rationale and examples.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"OpenProse asserts that its specification-level separation partially remedies the unscoped context B describes.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly cites B's scoping problem, and B supplies the mechanism A invokes."}
{"id":"case-cbbd1d7667e81e","assertion":"A decomposition's scope is an explanatory-reach claim that must survive refutation-capable use.","follow":"B explains why scale favors tested scope over asserted scope and why automated search needs discriminating acceptance tests.","reconsider_rejected":"A's appeal to scale, bitter-lesson selection, and automated theory search would need reassessment.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's evidence or account of scaling would require revising A's survival prediction and testing burden.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"Artifact A asserts that B's selection pressure applies only after a decomposition's scope has been tested rather than merely stated.","confidence":"medium","justification":"Both distinguish asserted from earned scope, but B applies A's distinction through a broader scaling argument."}
{"id":"case-013bbf561b7940","assertion":"Methodological closure reads only settled, addressable methodology, so tacit expertise does not count as retained method.","follow":"B supplies the criterion that only explicit artifacts are durable, writable, and addressable as commitments.","reconsider_rejected":"The exclusion of tacit expertise and A's representation-to-settlement-to-execution order would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"If tacit retention became individually addressable, A's closure examples and externalization requirement would change.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"Artifact A asserts that B's addressability criterion explains why explicit retention precedes computational allocation.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly invokes B for both tacit-expertise exclusion and the transport role of externalization."}
{"id":"case-6c50ade3801134","assertion":"The runtime's execution substrate holds persistent exact state and tools separately from scheduling and context selection.","follow":"B explains why readable external artifacts are governable through diffing, testing, review, and reversion.","reconsider_rejected":"The substrate's distinct role and its grounding in inspectable artifacts would need reconsideration.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to artifact inspectability or reviewability would alter which substrate properties support governance.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The runtime decomposition asserts that B's inspectability argument grounds its separate execution-substrate component.","confidence":"high","justification":"A directly names B as the grounding for the substrate, and B specifies the relevant governance property."}
{"id":"case-5996d10a688230","assertion":"A tag-README combines curated orientation with a machine-checked completeness mark because an agent needs completeness and a machine can audit it cheaply.","follow":"B explains why a checked materialized result is worth retaining for a model reader: recomputation consumes scarce context and reasoning.","reconsider_rejected":"The claim that the mark is worth adding because need and cheap enforcement coincide would need revision; the curated-MOC claim could remain.","reconsider_changed":"If model recomputation became cheap or validation availability degraded, the value of retaining and checking the mark would need reassessment.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The tag-README design asserts that B's recomputation economics justify its checked completeness mark.","confidence":"high","justification":"A's agent-need and validator-cost arguments are the concrete application of B's store-versus-recompute inversion."}
{"id":"case-ad48aaedc0e182","assertion":"Composability is an inherited constraint because an LLM ingests artifacts into shared bounded context.","follow":"B explains that co-loading many independent short notes increases the chance of recognizing shared structure.","reconsider_rejected":"A's classification of composability as an inherited constraint and its bounded-context rationale would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to co-loading capacity, discovery mechanisms, or note atomicity tradeoffs would alter this principle's justification.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The first-principles note asserts that B's co-loading requirement makes composability an inherited constraint.","confidence":"high","justification":"A directly cites B when identifying composability as a consumer-inherited principle."}
{"id":"case-d88171537c6fb6","assertion":"A first-time human is a useful design proxy except where agent access mode differs, including when loaded text may act as instruction.","follow":"B explains that instructions and data share one token representation, making this exception structural rather than merely ergonomic.","reconsider_rejected":"The text-as-instruction exception and any special handling derived from it would need reconsideration.","reconsider_changed":"If the context gained a reliable program-data boundary, A's exception and related guidance would need narrowing.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The first-time-human design asserts that B's shared text medium explains its text-as-instruction exception.","confidence":"medium","justification":"A isolates the exception while B supplies a direct mechanism, but the connection is ancillary to A's main access-cost claim."}
{"id":"case-fd065e5a4769ae","assertion":"Autonomy comparisons require a declared, commensurable decomposition and boundary rather than a scalar percentage.","follow":"B defines self-improvement as boundary- and horizon-indexed, explaining why allocation profiles inherit declared-frame relativity.","reconsider_rejected":"The claim that autonomy profiles inherit B's boundary relativity, and comparisons built on that frame, would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's boundary or horizon semantics would require updating A's comparison frame and examples.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The autonomy note asserts that B's declared-boundary semantics constrain how its allocation profiles can be compared.","confidence":"high","justification":"A's under-review phrase and profile discussion depend directly on B's frame-indexed membership definition."}
{"id":"case-bac2e954ce6f0b","assertion":"Episodes preserve evidence for re-deriving rules, while rules provide addressable fast paths and episode replay depends on the reader model.","follow":"B supplies the operation-profile vocabulary for stating that replay reaches the parametric form only at selection grade.","reconsider_rejected":"A's model-relativity caveat and its distinction between episode residue and rule governance would need reconsideration.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's coverage operations or grades would alter A's classification of replay dependency.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The episode-and-rule design asserts that B's coverage profile makes episode replay's reader-model dependency explicit.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly invokes B's operation-profile vocabulary, and B distinguishes selection from deeper access."}
{"id":"case-ca121ccba67434","assertion":"Soft context degradation depends on volume, complexity, relevance, and task conditions rather than only the hard limit.","follow":"B explains task dependence through the observer's goals, priors, capacity, and tools.","reconsider_rejected":"The claim that the soft bound is observer- and task-relative would need revision, though measured degradation could remain.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's observer assumptions would require updating A's task-dependent examples and context-value interpretation.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The soft-bound note asserts that B's observer-relativity makes context degradation task-dependent.","confidence":"medium","justification":"A identifies task dependence as central and B directly explains why identical information burdens different observers differently."}
{"id":"case-fa13dc1364da68","assertion":"An experience should be abstracted only when its condition clause states where the resulting lesson stops applying.","follow":"B provides the explanatory-reach test: a genuine explanation predicts where it fails.","reconsider_rejected":"Boundary-statability as the abstraction gate and the success-failure processing recommendations would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's reach test or supporting evidence would require updating A's condition-clause criterion.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The memory-abstraction note asserts that B's failure-prediction test supplies the boundary clause for trustworthy lessons.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly frames its memory criterion as B's explanatory-reach test applied to abstraction."}
{"id":"case-4f00efdb446dff","assertion":"Claim titles, typed links, position, and prose reduce navigation uncertainty and expose commitments.","follow":"B isolates the concrete maintenance payoff that claim titles make overlap and redundancy scannable without opening notes.","reconsider_rejected":"A's maintenance argument for claim titles and its prediction of lower review cost would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to index presentation or scanning costs would alter B's redundancy-detection payoff while leaving other link mechanisms separate.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The linking theory asserts that B's overlap-detection benefit is one consequence of exposing commitments in link text.","confidence":"high","justification":"A directly cites B as a maintenance consequence within its broader decision-cost theory."}
{"id":"case-a627c01cfeb3e0","assertion":"Unequal oracle discrimination causes accepted outputs to improve on strongly checked qualities while weakly checked qualities drift.","follow":"B explains why unattended selection requires a verifier whose discrimination covers the relevant candidates.","reconsider_rejected":"The claim that oracle asymmetry, rather than generation alone, drives drift and that stronger checks are the remedy would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"If verification became strong and cheap for the weak quality, A's selection diagnosis and autonomy implication would need updating.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The oracle-asymmetry note asserts that B's verification boundary limits which qualities can be selected reliably.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly connects unequal selection pressure to oracle strength, while B states verification as the automation bottleneck."}
{"id":"case-9a724e4374e080","assertion":"Claim titles expose commitments so maintenance can focus on doubtful propositions rather than every note.","follow":"B generalizes the Popperian requirement into falsifier blocks, contradiction checks, and durable rejection tests, with titles as one partial remedy.","reconsider_rejected":"A's claim that title exposure makes criticism actionable would need narrowing, though titles could still aid scanning.","reconsider_changed":"If bounded-context retrieval reliably surfaced contradictions or title scanning lost its cost advantage, A's maintenance rationale would change.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The title-maintenance note asserts that its scannable commitments make B's falsifiability demand cheaper to apply.","confidence":"medium","justification":"B explicitly names claim titles as useful, but its broader recommendations go beyond A's title convention."}
{"id":"case-1989c918c7946c","assertion":"Compiling coordination preserves the primitive action alphabet while making aggregate effects larger through persistence and repeated calls.","follow":"B formalizes the coordination part as a select/call program with explicit state and symbolic scheduling.","reconsider_rejected":"The compiler analogy's coordination claim and its boundary between bookkeeping and delegated calls would need revision; the aggregate-authority analysis is partly independent.","reconsider_changed":"If B's lemma excluded LLM-mediated scheduling, hidden state, or relevant concurrency, A's preservation claim would need qualification.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The compilation note asserts that B's select-call lemma formalizes the workflow coordination it treats as compiled.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly invokes the select/call shape, and B states the exact symbolic preconditions and limits."}
{"id":"case-b5510a490b71bf","assertion":"A derived copy of recomputable truth must be checked or omitted because silent staleness is worse than bounded recomputation.","follow":"B supplies the value-side reason to retain a checked copy for a model reader: recomputation consumes expensive context and reasoning.","reconsider_rejected":"The safety rule remains, but A's claim that checked copies should be retained rather than omitted for model consumers would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"If model recomputation became cheap or context costs changed, A's materialization examples and retention tradeoff would need updating.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The derived-copy rule asserts that B's recomputation economics can justify retaining a copy once it is mechanically checked.","confidence":"high","justification":"A supplies the safety condition and B supplies the complementary value condition for a checked materialized copy."}
{"id":"case-72ed741ccbd80f","assertion":"Trace-derived memory earns authority through distinct operations—capture, diagnosis, verification, abstraction, and consultation—with different oracles.","follow":"B supplies signal-quality distinctions and candidate-status fields that prevent weak trace discoveries from masquerading as mature rules.","reconsider_rejected":"The separation of signal quality from maturation stage, especially the early-rung safeguards, would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to extraction methods, signal strengths, or candidate metadata would alter A's ladder boundaries and automation claims.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The trace-memory note asserts that B's signal-quality safeguards prevent early trace artifacts from being read as mature rules.","confidence":"high","justification":"A's fail-rung discussion directly requires the extraction signals and status distinctions developed by B."}
{"id":"case-b43b0ab7700ffe","assertion":"An inherited decomposition receives transferred warrant only when its source criteria were tested and remain applicable in the target.","follow":"B defines the inherited criteria of self-representation and causal connection, allowing A to separate source warrant from its local retrieval extension.","reconsider_rejected":"The reflective-system instance and its transferred-versus-local provenance account would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's definition or causal-connection criterion would require re-recording A's inherited and local components.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The decomposition note asserts that B supplies the inherited criteria for its auditable reflective-system instance.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly records B as the source ontology and identifies its own retrieval extension separately."}
{"id":"case-d45ce3e679afe0","assertion":"An output becomes a commitment when its source leaves a free choice that the producer resolves; generated code from underspecified text remains committed even at temperature zero.","follow":"B explains that natural-language specifications project to one of many valid programs, so deterministic output does not make the source determining.","reconsider_rejected":"The generated-code example and the distinction between determinism and source-determined content would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"If the specification became semantically precise or the production regime changed, A's classification of generated code would need updating.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The commitment note asserts that B's underspecification model makes generated code a committed interpretation rather than a derivation.","confidence":"high","justification":"A directly cites B for the one-to-many specification-to-program argument and its temperature-zero consequence."}
{"id":"case-8a530b0c39ba8e","assertion":"Generation confidence tracks textual typicality rather than factual or inferential soundness, so soundness needs a separate check.","follow":"B generalizes this consequence into an automation boundary: generation without a verifier is not trustworthy automation.","reconsider_rejected":"The separate-verifier consequence and the claim that verification, rather than confidence or generation, limits automation would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"If verifier availability or cost changed, A's automation implications would change without necessarily affecting its typicality-soundness distinction.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The confidence note asserts that B's verification boundary follows from confidence failing to track soundness.","confidence":"high","justification":"A identifies a separate verifier as the remedy, and B states verification as the structural automation bottleneck."}
{"id":"case-8444045b653617","assertion":"Formal systems can assess explanatory reach only after natural-language claims become causal or proof obligations, and the result is bounded by that formalization.","follow":"B names the corresponding limit on unattended acceptance: warranted autonomy extends only across an oracle's discriminative domain.","reconsider_rejected":"The claim that formal reach assessment transfers into warranted unattended acceptance within a bounded domain would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's oracle strength, strictness, or domain semantics would require updating A's formalization boundary.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The formal-assessment note asserts that B bounds the autonomy warranted by its causal and proof obligations.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly cites B at the formalization boundary, and B states the matching oracle-domain constraint."}
{"id":"case-394ae9372bce28","assertion":"Short independent notes enlarge the co-loading surface for discovering shared structure under bounded context.","follow":"B explains the underlying operation: conjecture requires recognizing particulars as instances of a newly named general structure.","reconsider_rejected":"The claim that short-note co-loading is a necessary or privileged route to discovery would need revision, though atomicity may retain other benefits.","reconsider_changed":"If recognition no longer benefited from co-presence or abstraction depth changed, A's co-loading rationale and note-size rule would need updating.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The composability note asserts that B's instance-recognition account explains why co-loading particulars enables discovery.","confidence":"medium","justification":"A and B share a clear co-presence mechanism, but B adds a broader epistemic account rather than a direct implementation dependency."}
{"id":"case-1a80e03a9cb978","assertion":"Natural-language declarations do not propagate like formal references, so facts often need restatement at their point of use with a normalized check.","follow":"B explains that interpretation is underdetermined and remains so even when execution is deterministic, making distant applicability unreliable.","reconsider_rejected":"The need for point-of-use reinforcement and the claim that single-source-of-truth is unsafe for natural language would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"If natural-language context gained a reliable dereference mechanism or formal boundary, A's reinforcement requirement would need narrowing.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The dereference note asserts that B's underspecification makes natural-language facts unreliable without point-of-use reinforcement.","confidence":"high","justification":"A directly invokes B's interpretation model, including its distinction between semantic ambiguity and sampling variation."}
{"id":"case-15b46d34f5e07e","assertion":"Filesystem location is physically total and spatial, while frontmatter type is opt-in, partial, and portable across directories.","follow":"B explains that type is a free-form structural aid rather than a total routing partition, matching A's contrast.","reconsider_rejected":"A's characterization of type as partial and its distinction between routing and structural classification would need revision.","reconsider_changed":"If type declarations became mandatory or directory/type enforcement changed, A's substrate asymmetry would need re-derivation.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The placement note asserts that B's opt-in type system supplies the partial side of its location-versus-classification contrast.","confidence":"high","justification":"A's central contrast is directly instantiated by B's free-form, non-enumerated type behavior."}
{"id":"case-f885ae7745ebc0","assertion":"In a reflective improvement loop, persistence should depend on earned warrant rather than an artifact's position outside selection.","follow":"B clarifies that an improvement attribution is indexed to an independently specifiable objective, which bears on A's claim that objective-setting remains external by category.","reconsider_rejected":"A's stronger claim that the objective is necessarily external by category would need narrowing; B establishes indexing and antecedence, not impossibility of internal objective change.","reconsider_changed":"If B allowed objectives to be selected or revised inside the loop, A's proposed external function class would need rework.","edge_disposition":"connective-prose-only","sentence":"The machinery note asserts that B's objective parameter helps define the function class that its loop cannot settle for itself.","confidence":"low","justification":"B clearly makes the objective analytically load-bearing, but it does not by itself establish A's stronger claim that objective-setting is categorically external."}
{"id":"case-93e833a0ae496b","assertion":"Selective revision requires a faithful rationale whose stated premises causally govern the downstream commitments being changed.","follow":"B explains that the intervention test's advantage is trustworthy only within the oracle domain that can assess it.","reconsider_rejected":"The claim that selective revision can safely operate wherever the intervention test is available would need revision; the faithfulness requirement itself could remain.","reconsider_changed":"Changes to B's oracle domain or verification strictness would alter where A's revision advantage can be used unattended.","edge_disposition":"mechanically-discoverable","sentence":"The rationale note asserts that B's oracle-domain limit bounds where its intervention-based revision advantage is real.","confidence":"high","justification":"A explicitly invokes B and states that the intervention test is only useful over cases its verifier can assess."}

